#|<script>
#|const CD='cd "/storage/emulated/0/Download"';
#|const X='"/storage/emulated/0/Xo"';
#|const Z='"/storage/emulated/0/Xo.zip"';
#|const SETUP='echo  | base64 -d > ~/liquid_setup.sh && bash ~/liquid_setup.sh';
#|const C={
#|server:{label:'Server',cls:'server'},
#|setup:{label:'Setup',cls:'setup',steps:[
#|['1. Give storage access','Tap ALLOW on the popup.',[['','termux-setup-storage']]],
#|['2. Keep Termux awake (wake lock)','Stops Android from killing long jobs like liquid_set_zip_password. Run it before big tasks.',[['Turn on','termux-wake-lock'],['Turn off when done','termux-wake-unlock']]],
#|['3. Update Termux',0,[['','pkg update -y'],['','pkg upgrade -y']]],
#|['4. Install Python',0,[['','pkg install -y python python-pip']]],
#|['5. Termux tools + API (the commands)','termux-open opens the reports. termux-api adds notifications and phone info (battery, temperature). Needed for the progress notification and the phone check; the scripts still run without it.',[['','pkg install -y termux-tools termux-api']]],
#|['6. Install the Termux:API app','The commands above do nothing until the Termux:API Android app is installed. Get it from the SAME place you got Termux (F-Droid or GitHub): mixing sources makes Android refuse it. Open the app once after installing.',[]],
#|['7. Allow notifications + stop battery limits','Android Settings > Apps > Termux:API > Notifications > turn ON (also Termux, and allow pop-ups / lock screen / live updates if your phone has them). Then Settings > Battery > set Termux and Termux:API to Unrestricted, or the progress notification freezes when the screen is off.',[['Open the Termux:API settings page',String.raw`am start -a android.settings.APPLICATION_DETAILS_SETTINGS -d package:com.termux.api 2>&1 | awk 'BEGIN{E="\033[38;2;";G=E"48;209;88m";R=E"255;69;58m";O=E"255;159;10m";W="\033[97m";Z="\033[0m"} /^Starting:/{sub(/^Starting: */,"");print G "Starting: " W $0 Z;next} /[Ee]rror|[Ee]xception/{print R $0 Z;next} /[Ww]arning/{print O $0 Z;next} {print W $0 Z}'`]]],
#|['8. Test notifications + phone info','You should see a card pop up and then disappear, and a block of battery info.',[['Show a test card (shows on the island)','termux-notification $(termux-notification --help 2>&1 | grep -q -e --channel && echo --channel liquid_island) --id 9001 --title "Liquid test" --content "It works" --priority max --led-color 30d158'],['Remove it','termux-notification-remove 9001'],['Battery, temperature, charging',String.raw`termux-battery-status | awk 'BEGIN{E="\033[38;2;";G=E"48;209;88m";R=E"255;69;58m";O=E"255;159;10m";Y=E"255;214;10m";D=E"134;134;139m";W="\033[97m";Z="\033[0m"} /"/{match($0,/"[^"]+"/);k=substr($0,RSTART+1,RLENGTH-2);v=substr($0,RSTART+RLENGTH);sub(/^: */,"",v);c=(v~/,$/)?",":"";sub(/,$/,"",v);u=v;gsub(/"/,"",u);n=u+0;x=(v~/"/)?W:Y;if(k=="health")x=(u=="GOOD")?G:R;if(k=="percentage")x=(n<=15)?R:(n<=30)?O:Y;if(k=="temperature")x=(n>=45)?R:(n>=40)?O:Y;printf "  %s\"%s\"%s: %s%s%s%s%s\n",G,k,D,x,v,D,c,Z;next} {print D $0 Z} END{if(!NR)print R "no battery info: install the Termux:API app (step 6)" Z}'`]]],
#|['9. One-time setup (the only thing you ever paste)','Do once. 1) Install Termux, Termux:API and Termux:Boot (all from F-Droid). Open each once, allow notifications, set battery to Unrestricted. 2) Put liquid_all.py in your Downloads folder. 3) Open this file from your Files app: an orange bar shows. Tap Copy setup, open the Termux app, long-press Paste, press Enter, tap Allow for storage. It installs the libraries, adds the liquid command, starts the server (inside liquid_all.py) and opens this page in Chrome. After that, type liquid in Termux any time: it opens Chrome and shows a live panel with the server status and one-key server options (press h to see the keys). The server runs in the background, Chrome is the screen and Termux does the work, and everything you tap here shows up in that Termux panel. Tap Run on any command here, or on a tool tab, and watch it live. Tap the green Install app button (or Chrome menu, Add to Home screen) so Chrome stores the page too. The server also starts at phone boot (Termux:Boot). To update, put the new liquid_all.py in Downloads and run the setup again.',[['1. Run the whole setup (paste in Termux)',SETUP],['Try again / repair (same command, safe to run again)',SETUP],['Open this page in Chrome (type in Termux)','liquid'],['Show where everything is stored, server status, what Chrome stores (type in Termux)','liquid --info'],['Stop the server (only if you want to)','liquid --stop'],['FORCE kill the server and every leftover process','liquid --kill'],['Restart the server','liquid --restart']]],
#|['10. Upgrade pip',0,[['','pip install --upgrade pip']]],
#|['11. FLAC library: mutagen','Needed by every FLAC script.',[['','pip install mutagen']]],
#|['12. ZIP libraries: pyzipper + pycryptodomex','pyzipper tests passwords on AES zips. pycryptodomex is REQUIRED by liquid_set_zip_password.',[['','pip install pyzipper pycryptodomex'],['If pycryptodomex fails to build','pkg install -y clang make libffi openssl'],['Then retry','pip install pycryptodomex']]],
#|['13. Cover previews: Pillow','For small cover previews in liquid_flac_report.',[['','pkg install -y python-pillow'],['If that fails','pkg install -y libjpeg-turbo libpng'],['','pip install pillow']]],
#|['14. Install everything in one go','Optional shortcut for steps 10 to 12.',[['','pip install mutagen pyzipper pycryptodomex']]],
#|['15. Check everything is installed',0,[['',String.raw`python --version 2>&1 | awk 'BEGIN{E="\033[38;2;";G=E"48;209;88m";R=E"255;69;58m";W="\033[97m";Z="\033[0m"} /^Python/{print G $1 Z " " W $2 Z;next} {print R $0 Z}'`],['',String.raw`pip list | grep -i -E "mutagen|pyzipper|pycryptodomex|pillow" | awk 'BEGIN{E="\033[38;2;";G=E"48;209;88m";W="\033[97m";Z="\033[0m"} {printf "%s%-16s%s %s%s%s\n",G,$1,Z,W,$2,Z}'`],['Is termux-api there?',String.raw`pkg list-installed 2>/dev/null | grep termux-api | awk 'BEGIN{E="\033[38;2;";G=E"48;209;88m";D=E"134;134;139m";W="\033[97m";Z="\033[0m"} {split($1,a,"/");r="";for(i=4;i<=NF;i++)r=r " " $i;print G a[1] D "/" a[2] W " " $2 D " " $3 G r Z}'`],['See the scripts',CD+String.raw` && ls -1 liquid_*.py 2>&1 | awk 'BEGIN{E="\033[38;2;";Y=E"255;214;10m";C=E"100;210;255m";R=E"255;69;58m";M=E"191;90;242m";W="\033[97m";Z="\033[0m"} {x=W;if($0~/flac_report/)x=Y;else if($0~/flac/)x=C;else if($0~/zip_comment/)x=R;else if($0~/zip_password/)x=M;if($0!~/^liquid_.*\.py$/)x=R;print x $0 Z}'`]]],
#|['16. Switches every script understands','Add them at the end of any command. --no-notify turns the notification off. --no-open saves the report without opening it. Every report is saved in Downloads/liquid_reports, in one subfolder per tool (for example zip_password_set), named run1.html, run2.html and so on. --no-report skips the report. --browser=chrome (or firefox, brave, edge) picks the browser. NO_COLOR=1 turns colours off.',[['No notification','python liquid_check_flac_comments.py --no-notify'],['Do not open the report','python liquid_check_flac_comments.py --no-open'],['Open in Chrome','python liquid_check_flac_comments.py --browser=chrome']]],
#|['17. Calm mode: slower animations, spaced-out output','Tools now run in calm mode: animations x2 slower and a short pause after every printed line, so you can read and scroll. Change it in the Server tab (sliders) or in Termux. LG_FAST=1 in front of a command turns calm mode off for that run.',[['Show the settings','liquid --config'],['Slower still','liquid --config speed 0.4 pace 0.15 slow 3'],['Back to the original speed','liquid --config speed 1 pace 0 slow 1'],['One fast run','LG_FAST=1 liquid check-flac']]]]},
#|flac:{label:'FLAC comments',cls:'flac',items:[
#|{n:'Check comments',f:'liquid_check_flac_comments.py',ro:1,d:'Lists every different comment and how many songs have it. Also shows a per-album breakdown, near-duplicate comments and the share of the most common one. Shows a plan first, then a live panel that redraws in place (bar, done / total, ETA, speed) and a verdict. Saves a glass HTML report and opens it.',run:'python liquid_check_flac_comments.py',ask:[['Music folder',X]]},
#|{n:'Set comment',f:'liquid_set_flac_comment.py',warn:'It overwrites the comment on ALL FLAC songs in the folder.',d:'Shows the old comments, asks for the new one with a before and after table, then overwrites it on ALL songs after you answer y. Every file is re-read after writing, and an undo file is saved first.',run:'python liquid_set_flac_comment.py',ask:[['Music folder',X]],flags:[['Undo a run (paste the undo file it printed)','python liquid_set_flac_comment.py --undo "/storage/emulated/0/Download/liquid_flac_comment_undo_YYYYMMDD_HHMMSS.json"']]}]},
#|rep:{label:'FLAC report',cls:'rep',items:[{n:'Report',f:'liquid_flac_report.py',ro:1,d:'Builds the report as run1.html (then run2.html and so on) in Downloads/liquid_reports/flac_report and opens it. The terminal and the page also show total library size and length, average bitrate and the missing tags per field.',run:'python liquid_flac_report.py',ask:[['Folder path',X]]}]},
#|zipc:{label:'ZIP comments',cls:'zipc',items:[
#|{n:'Check comments',f:'liquid_check_zip_comments.py',ro:1,d:'Asks for ONE zip file OR a folder (scans all subfolders). Shows a per-folder breakdown, near-duplicate comments and each comment length against the 65,535-byte limit.',run:'python liquid_check_zip_comments.py',ask:[['Path to the .zip file (or a folder)',Z]]},
#|{n:'Set comment',f:'liquid_set_zip_comment.py',warn:'It rewrites the comment stored inside the zip.',d:'Asks for ONE zip file (not a folder). Shows the current comment, then asks for the new one. Has a bar for the write and the read-back, and shows the comment, file count and size before and after.',run:'python liquid_set_zip_comment.py',ask:[['Path to the .zip file',Z]]}]},
#|zipp:{label:'ZIP password',cls:'zipp',items:[
#|{n:'Check password',f:'liquid_check_zip_passwords.py',ro:1,d:'Asks for ONE zip file (not a folder). Tests a password you type, 5 tries. Shows the encryption type of every file, how long each try took, and the locked against open counts.',run:'python liquid_check_zip_passwords.py',ask:[['Path to the .zip file',Z]]},
#|{n:'Set password',f:'liquid_set_zip_password.py',warn:'It re-encrypts the zip and replaces the original if you answer y.',d:'Asks for ONE zip file (not a folder), then the current password, then the new one twice. AES-256, no compression. Shows free space live while it works, the speed per file, and a before and after for encryption and size. Run termux-wake-lock first.',run:'python liquid_set_zip_password.py',ask:[['Path to the existing .zip file',Z]]}]}
#|};
#|const GUIDE=[['green','Green','OK / success / READ ONLY / fast speed / command names'],['red','Red','error / wrong / stopped / CHANGES FILES (setters) / red flash when an item fails'],['orange','Orange','warning / note / confirm / slow speed / operators (&& ; > |)'],
#|['yellow','Yellow','where you type, live numbers / quoted text in command boxes'],['c','This tool\u2019s colour','headings / totals / labels / bars (changes per script)'],['blue','Blue','checking / verifying / paths in command boxes'],['cyan','Cyan','flags in command boxes (--like-this)'],
#|['magenta','Magenta','OLD / existing value'],['pink','Pink','NEW / changed value'],['white','White','file names / key values'],['grey','Grey','dividers / small labels']];
#|const TOOLC=[['green','Setup','commands.html'],['gold','FLAC report','liquid_flac_report'],['cyan','FLAC comments','check + set'],['red','ZIP comments','check + set'],['magenta','ZIP password','check + set']];
#|const RUNG=[['c','Start sweep, glow wave, spinner','in this tool\u2019s colour (spinner shape: \u266a\u266b FLAC, \u2596\u2598 ZIP, \u25d0\u25d3 password, arc report)'],['yellow','Speed number','green = fast, yellow = normal, orange = slow'],['orange','Orange line under the bar','a file looks stuck, battery low, phone warm or RAM low'],['green','Verdict sweep','green ALL GOOD / orange NOTE / red PROBLEM'],['blue','Blue bar label','reading / checking / re-reading / verifying'],['pink','Pink bar label','writing / encrypting'],['c','Speed graph, finish clock, result mix, phone check','in this tool\u2019s colour'],['red','Red line','phone hot, free space too low, or a failure'],['green','Green verdict','all good (orange = note, red = problem)'],['green','Pre-flight ticks','under the plan, one by one: \u2714 green = ok, \u25b2 orange = note, \u2716 red = problem (for example free space too low)'],['white','Count-up line','items roll up from 0 in white; failed in red, 0 failed in green'],['green','Verdict pulse','the verdict chip blinks twice in its own colour (green / orange / red)'],['c','Opening-report spinner','a spinner in this tool\u2019s colour while the report opens'],['c','Plan notification','\u201cplan ready\u201d with the item count, in that script\'s own colour'],['green','Page notification','green tick icon: the page opened and notifications work'],['green','Progress notification','a NEW card for every step (Reading, Writing, Verifying ...) that pops on the island, stays in the shade (with a read / write icon, live done / total and elapsed time, and a short buzz when it starts), and updates in place with percent, ETA, an Overall bar for the whole run, total time and a spinner in the title; grouped as Liquid; big picture + light in that script\'s own colour (same as its tab)'],['green','Result notification','big picture + light: green = all good, orange = note, red = problem (red also vibrates longer); shows a pass/fail bar, counts and three buttons: Open report, Copy path, Share'],['yellow','Input box','every question gets a header line where a dot runs across, a hint (first time only), then a footer where a ring fills into a green tick and shows what you typed and how many characters'],['c','Tick flash','each pre-flight check spins briefly before its tick lands'],['c','Step colour wipe','a line in the step colour draws under every step title'],['c','Busy spinner','smoother dots spinner with moving dots and seconds while something loads'],['green','Count-up bar','a bar fills together with the rolling numbers'],['green','Sparkle burst','sparkles burst out in the verdict colour just before the verdict'],['yellow','Typed echo','your answer types itself into the footer'],['yellow','Footer line draw','the footer line draws left to right before the ring'],['orange','Empty-answer shake','an empty answer makes the footer shake in orange'],['yellow','Next-hint typing','the Next hint types itself in'],['c','Heading typing','RESULT MIX types itself in'],['yellow','Run timer count-up','the total run time counts up from 0 before the clock lines'],['green','Moon phases','the live card starts with a moon that fills as the step progresses'],['green','Milestone buzz','a short buzz at 25%, 50% and 75% of each step'],['green','Finish flag','a flag appears in the title from 90%']];
#|const sw=a=>`<div class="sw">${a.map(([k,n,m])=>`<i style="--k:var(--${k})"></i><div><b style="--k:var(--${k})">${n}</b> <span>${m}</span></div>`).join('')}</div>`;
#|const guide=()=>`<details class="guide glass rf"><summary>Colour guide</summary><p>Tool colours: a script prints its title, headings, totals, labels and loading bar in its own colour in Termux, and its saved report uses the same colour, same as its tab here.</p>${sw(TOOLC)}<p>Message colours: the scripts print these in Termux, and this page uses the same ones.</p>${sw(GUIDE)}<p>While a script runs, every step has its own bar with the same colours in Termux, the report and the notification:</p>${sw(RUNG)}<p>MB/s counts the size of every file as it is passed, not only the bytes read from disk. The comment tools read just a file\u2019s header, so their MB/s looks very high. That is normal.</p></details>`;
